[
  {
    "sys_consistent_procedure": "My rule is simple: if I can stop someone getting hurt without hurting anyone else, I do it, even when it's awkward",
    "ce_mentalizing_difficulty": "I honestly can't tell what's going through their heads.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "Somebody should have chocked those wheels before walking away."
  },
  {
    "sys_consistent_procedure": "I keep one test for moments like this: does acting spare harm and cost nobody else anything? If it does, I act",
    "ce_mentalizing_difficulty": "I can't work out what they meant by it.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "A locked handbrake and a second person checking would have stopped this."
  },
  {
    "sys_consistent_procedure": "I go by one habit: if the harm in front of me can be stopped at no cost to anyone, I stop it",
    "ce_mentalizing_difficulty": "I'm struggling to make sense of the five of them",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "Track work should always have a lookout posted for exactly this."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "my hands would probably be shaking.",
    "sys_consistent_procedure": "I ask two things: who gets hurt if I act, and who gets hurt if I don't.",
    "ce_mentalizing_difficulty": "What I can't work out is whoever put a lever within reach",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "What did they expect a passenger to do with it? I really can't say."
  },
  {
    "sys_consistent_procedure": "Same rule every time: if nobody pays for it and people are spared, I act",
    "ce_mentalizing_difficulty": "I genuinely can't read them.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "The crew should have radioed the station before stepping onto the line"
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "my chest is tight thinking about it.",
    "sys_consistent_procedure": "My method is to line up who gets hurt under each option",
    "ce_mentalizing_difficulty": "the workers are what I can't figure out.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "Catch points on that stretch would have made this impossible."
  },
  {
    "sys_consistent_procedure": "I hold myself to one thing: when stepping in stops people getting hurt and endangers nobody, I step in",
    "ce_mentalizing_difficulty": "I can't work out what they had in mind",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "An interlock that automatically sends runaway stock into that siding should have been fitted."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "my legs would go.",
    "sys_consistent_procedure": "I use the same yardstick I'd use at home: if it's cheap for me and it keeps others safe, do it.",
    "ce_mentalizing_difficulty": "I try to work out what's going on in their heads and I just can't",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "A proper stop-block and a signal at that end of the yard should have been installed"
  },
  {
    "sys_consistent_procedure": "My approach is to look at what each option does to the people involved and go with whichever harms nobody.",
    "ce_mentalizing_difficulty": "I can't read whoever left that train able to roll.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "The depot should have required two sign-offs before any empty train was left unattended."
  },
  {
    "sys_consistent_procedure": "My procedure is to spell out who is affected under each choice",
    "ce_mentalizing_difficulty": "I can't tell what's in their minds",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "A warning horn fitted to that stretch, sounding whenever rolling stock moves unattended, would have helped."
  }
]
